@BerndNK 

This issue is tracked with https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/19794. I'll close this one as a duplicate but feel free to send any response or question we can help with. 

We don't recommend using the `ToSerializedString` and we are planning to obsolete it. Now we have time zones covering all world and every zone. We recommend you just serialize the zone Id and then create `TimeZoneInfo` from that Id instead. `ToSerializedString` was originally designed around Windows time zone and it is not suitable to use on Linux based systems. I guess the differences you are seeing is because running on Windows against Linux.
